# AI policy

Full text: `doc/AI_POLICY.md` (adapted from Bitcoin Core). High bar for all contributions.

## Required behavior

- Human author in the loop: choose the work, own the contribution, and be able to explain effects.
- Do not open or drive pull requests autonomously.
- Do not set an agent as git author or co-author.
- Do not draft GitHub issue/PR comments or review replies meant to be posted as-is; humans write those in their own words.
- Only propose changes the human can defend (what changed, why, how it was verified).

## How humans may own the change

Understanding need not mean line-by-line reading of every file. A testing-led loop is fine: design cases, run builds/tests, fail/fix with the agent, ship only what you verified. For funds-touching code, prefer reading the shipped diff plus tests over trusting green CI alone.

## Disclosure

If AI interaction context is useful in a comment, it must be disclosed and paired with human commentary on relevance and implications.

## Agent practice

Prefer small, reviewable diffs and help the human verify (cargo test, blackbox paths, checklists). Leave PR bodies, review answers, and commit authorship to the human. Violations can get PRs closed without notice.
